Expleo is a trusted partner for your innovation journey. As a global engineering, technology and consulting service provider, we are ideally positioned to help you achieve your ambitions and future-proof your business. With a smart blend of bold thinking and reliable execution, we’re able to fast-track innovation through each step of your value chain.

We are strategically positioned to build value, with a global footprint across 30 countries.

We are as global and local as you need us to be, with strong best-in-class pan-European technological centres and unique best-shoring capabilities.

We leverage a network of high value-adding affiliates in consulting and industrial excellence, and leading partners across multiple sectors to provide you with the most comprehensive services and solutions in an ever-changing environment.

Responsibilities

We are looking for a data analyst who can also develop practical tools.

The main responsibility is to analyze operational data from tolling and intelligent transportation products.

The candidate will use SQL and Excel to prepare data, investigate results, identify problems and communicate findings.

The candidate will use Python, Linux, and scripting to build small utilities and repeatable workflows.

Data Analysis

Essential skills


Practical professional experience analyzing data;
Good working knowledge of SQL;
Good working knowledge of Excel, including formulas, filters, pivot tables, and charts;
Ability to clean, compare, summarize, and validate data;
Ability to identify inconsistencies, patterns, and outliers;
Ability to explain findings clearly to technical and non-technical people.


Development Support


Practical experience with Python;
Familiarity with Linux and command-line tools;
Familiarity with scripting and task automation;
Ability to create or adapt small tools that make analysis faster or more reliable.


Desired Skills


Strong analytical skills and critical-thinking ability;
Careful and methodical when handling data;
Able to question assumptions, assess evidence, and distinguish facts from interpretations;
Able to document assumptions, steps, and conclusions;
Highly autonomous and accountable for progressing work independently;
Comfortable working in an exploratory environment where the problem and expected outcome may not always be fully scoped;
Comfortable collaborating with software and operations teams;
Good communication in English, spoken and written.
Show more

We are looking for a data analyst who can also develop practical tools. The main responsibility is to analyze operational data from tolling and intelligent transportation products. The candidate will use SQL and Excel to prepare data, investigate results, identify problems, and communicate findings. When analysis work benefits from automation, the candidate will use Python, Linux, and scripting to build small utilities and repeatable workflows. This is primarily a data-analysis role, not a general software-development role.

What The Candidate Must Have

Data analysis


Practical professional experience analyzing data;
Good working knowledge of SQL;
Good working knowledge of Excel, including formulas, filters, pivot tables, and charts;
Ability to clean, compare, summarize, and validate data;
Ability to identify inconsistencies, patterns, and outliers;
Ability to explain findings clearly to technical and non-technical people.


Development support


Practical experience with Python;
Familiarity with Linux and command-line tools;
Familiarity with scripting and task automation;
Ability to create or adapt small tools that make analysis faster or more reliable.


Working style


Strong analytical skills and critical-thinking ability;
Careful and methodical when handling data;
Able to question assumptions, assess evidence, and distinguish facts from interpretations;
Able to document assumptions, steps, and conclusions;
Highly autonomous and accountable for progressing work independently;
Comfortable working in an exploratory environment where the problem and expected outcome may not always be fully scoped;
Comfortable collaborating with software and operations teams;
Good communication in English, spoken and written.


Typical work


Query and analyze operational data using SQL;
Use Excel to explore data, produce summaries, and communicate results;
Check data quality and investigate unexpected results;
Compare data from different systems or sources;
Prepare concise reports and recommendations;
Automate repetitive preparation and analysis tasks with Python and scripts;
Use Linux tools to inspect files, logs, and data-processing jobs;
Build lightweight utilities to support analysis when needed;
Keep analysis steps and results understandable to other team members.


Useful, But Not Required


Experience with Python data-analysis libraries such as pandas;
Experience with operational, event, sensor, image, or other high-volume data;
Experience working with software, systems, or operations teams;
Familiarity with Git;
Experience in tolling or intelligent transportation.


These are advantages, not mandatory requirements. Candidates should not be excluded because they lack a specific framework, database product, degree, or software-development methodology if they can demonstrate the core skills above.

Company Context


International company working on tolling and intelligent transportation products;
Work location: Lagoas Park, Oeiras;
Collaboration with software, systems, data, and operations teams;
Documentation and collaboration in English and Portuguese;
The required development and data environments will be provided.
Show more

Purpose of Position

The Business Insights Analyst Associate combines analytical knowledge and aptitude with adaptability, practicality, and a strong ability to communicate. The purpose is to deliver exceptional analytical insights and solutions to challenges throughout NetJets.

This role is responsible for gathering, managing and consolidating accurate information to provide to the business within the diverse areas that belong to the Business Insights & Analytics department, executing analysis measuring the business performance.

This role will help define solutions and support change adoption to improve forecasting performance, cross functional communication, and integrated planning.

Tasks And Responsibilities


Develop and implement company dashboard reports, analytical modelling and visualizations to facilitate the monitoring of the business, allowing to quickly identify and act on issues and seize opportunities;
Assist to identify key business indicators to enhance the understanding of key business stakeholders of business needs by the distribution and creation of reporting, analysis, mining, visualization, dashboards, whilst proposing solutions to business concerns;
Provide data and create timely, relevant, and accurate analyses of operational and business data and processes at the level of fidelity required for the diverse areas of the business;
Provides expertise in statistics, data visualization, machine learning, mathematical optimization, simulation, or another analytical specialty;
Learn new tools and techniques as needed to produce the best possible results;
Perform analysis of both strategic and tactical business and operational questions while working independently, pragmatically, and with reliance on creative analytical curiosity;
Collaborate with business partners to analytically explore business and operational problems. Gather and act to resolve operational issues through increasing business acumen;
Help simplify complex analytical models/insights/solutions in presentations for Executive Leadership Team;
Author memos or presentations summarizing/explaining insights effectively;
Practice active listening and seeks feedback routinely to build business partner relationships and to foster trust in analytical insights and the recommendations of decision support tools and analyses.


Education

Bachelor's in Computer Science or Mathematics

Certifications and Licenses

Years Of Experience

0-2 years of experience

Core Competencies

Service-Oriented

Curiosity

Collaboration

Adaptability

Strives For Positive Results

Knowledge, Skills, Abilities And Other (KSAOs)


University degree in Computer Science, Management, Mathematics, Statistics or similar;
From 0 to 2 years of experience in a similar role or related work experience (preferential in aviation industry);
Ability to demonstrate high level of business acumen and commercial attitude;
Analytical skills with demonstrated experience in creating data architectures and datasets, machine learning and algorithms, prescriptive and predictive modelling techniques, advanced statistical techniques (regression, statistical tests etc) and their various applications;
High Proficiency in MS Office (VBA preferably) and experience in an analytical platform such as SAS, Python, AWS, SQL, R, or CRM solutions (SalesForce), and visualization platform such as Tableau, Qlik, Power BI;
Exceptional creative problem-solving abilities;
Detail oriented and proven ability to prioritize multiple objectives in a dynamic environment with constantly shifting priorities;
Initiative, confidence, and the drive to achieve results without explicit direction or detailed instruction;
Fluency in Business English (written and spoken).
Show more

Learn About Knok

At knok, we dare to lead and humanise the digital transformation of healthcare. We envision a world where everyone has timely access to quality healthcare through digital technology, creating a more equal society. We genuinely believe in it, and you can recognise it in every person who embraces this mission.

Through a Digital Front Door strategy, knok connects patients, providers and healthcare professionals in one place. Our API-first white-label platform enables a continuous, engaging and personalised healthcare experience for all conditions through a cutting-edge Patient Journey Engine.

With regular clinical practice as our main source of knowledge, we leverage ready-to-use data to improve care automation and increase financial savings. Since 2015, we have enabled more than 2.5 million clinical interactions in over 12 countries. Our platform is scalable and AI-ready, enhancing the power of data-driven care to deliver better outcomes during all stages of life.

Are you ready to join us in revolutionising healthcare and making a tangible impact on people's lives?

About The Role

We are looking for a Junior Healthcare Data Analyst to support our teams in turning complex healthcare data into meaningful insights. You'll be working with datasets from different sources, such as clinical operations, insurance processing, and patient journeys - helping us improve care delivery and decision-making.

If you're passionate about using data to make healthcare more accessible and effective, don't stop here - dive deeper!

As an Junior Healthcare Data Analyst, you will:


Collect, clean, and analyse healthcare data from multiple sources (e.g. EHR, patient demographics, operational systems), to extract meaningful insights;
Develop and maintain dashboards, reports, and visualisations to communicate key metrics and findings to stakeholders, including clinicians, operational teams and leadership team;
Collaborate cross-functionally with teams across the organisation, including data science, product management, and clinical operations, to support data-driven decision-making;
Perform statistical analysis to support population health management, risk stratification, and clinical outcome optimisation;
Contribute to improving data quality by identifying data quality issues and anomalies, and work with relevant stakeholders to address and resolve them


What Makes You a Great Fit For This Journey


Bachelor's degree in Biomedical Engineering, Medical Statistics, Biomedical Sciences, Data Science, Statistics, Computer Science, Health Informatics, or a related field. Master's degree preferred;
Experience (academic or professional) with data visualisation tools such as Tableau, Power BI or similar;
Technical expertise regarding data models, database design development, data mining and segmentation techniques;
Ability to turn complex data into clear insights that support better decision-making;
Knowledge of programming languages such as Python or R for data analysis and statistical modeling;
Ability to explain a dashboard or an analysis to someone without a technical background, in a simple and practical way;
Care when working with data to ensure accuracy, consistency and reliability;
Ability to manage several analytical tasks at the same time, prioritising what has the greatest impact on the business and patients


Nice to have:


Experience with SQL;
Experience with Apache Superset;
Previous experience or exposure to the healthcare sector


Recruitment stages


People Interview: A conversation to get to know you better, explore your background and motivation, and introduce you to knok, our culture, and the role.
Case Study: A practical exercise designed to understand how you approach data, structure your analysis, and turn information into meaningful insights.
Final Interview: A conversation with the Hiring Manager where you'll present your case study, explain your reasoning, and discuss your approach in more detail
